{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1392274,"ns":0,"title":"Lazy argument","extract":"The lazy argument or idle argument (Ancient Greek: ἀργὸς λόγος) is an attempt to undermine the philosophical doctrine of fatalism by demonstrating that, if everything that happens is determined by fate, it is futile to take any kind of action. Its basic form is that of a complex constructive dilemma.","description":"Philosophical view","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}